Subject: setjmp: define the __c_longjmp tag
Last-Update: 2026-09-27

`__wasm_longjmp()` throws with the `__c_longjmp` WebAssembly tag. clang 21
and older define that tag, weakly, in every object that throws or catches
with it; clang 22 and later leave the definition to the C library, so with
them a module that links the setjmp/longjmp runtime fails on an undefined
`__c_longjmp`. The tag, with one pointer-sized parameter, is now defined
here in inline assembly for clang 22 and later; older compilers are left to
define it as they did.

This is wasi-libc's fix, from commit 2fc32bc81b9f ("Test with LLVM 22 in CI,
fix a setjmp/longjmp issue", https://github.com/WebAssembly/wasi-libc/pull/772,
by alexcrichton, 2026-03-11), applied to wasix-libc's copy of the runtime.

diff --git a/libc-top-half/musl/src/setjmp/setjmplongjmp.c b/libc-top-half/musl/src/setjmp/setjmplongjmp.c
--- a/libc-top-half/musl/src/setjmp/setjmplongjmp.c
+++ b/libc-top-half/musl/src/setjmp/setjmplongjmp.c
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
+// Modified for ServiceCache: backported fix of https://github.com/WebAssembly/wasi-libc/pull/772
 #ifndef __wasilibc_unmodified_upstream
 #include <setjmp.h>
 
@@ -79,6 +80,24 @@ __wasm_longjmp(void *env, int val)
         __builtin_wasm_throw(1, arg); /* 1 == C_LONGJMP */
 }
 
+// The `__builtin_wasm_throw` invocation above will reference this symbol which
+// refers to a WebAssembly tag. The tag can't be defined in C but we can define
+// it with inline assembly, so do so here.
+//
+// Note that the means of defining this symbol changed historically, so this
+// is only done on LLVM 22+ where it's required.
+#if __clang_major__ >= 22
+__asm__(".globl __c_longjmp\n"
+#if defined(__wasm32__)
+        ".tagtype __c_longjmp i32\n"
+#elif defined(__wasm64__)
+        ".tagtype __c_longjmp i64\n"
+#else
+#error "Unsupported Wasm architecture"
+#endif
+        "__c_longjmp:\n");
+#endif
+
 #  else
 
 #include <wasi/libc.h>
